    {
      "text": "he maketh his sun to rise on the evil and on the good, Matt. 5:45 (3 Ne. 12:45). children shall rise up against their parents, Matt. 10:21 (Mark 13:12). hath not risen a greater than John the Baptist, Matt. 11:11. John … is risen from the dead, Matt. 14:2 (Mark 6:14; Luke 9:7). Tell … no man, until the Son of man be risen, Matt. 17:9 (Mark 9:9). third day he shall rise again, Matt. 20:19 (27:63; Mark 8:31; 9:31; 10:34; Luke 18:33; 1 Cor. 15:4; Mosiah 3:10). nation shall rise against nation, Matt. 24:7 (Mark 13:8; Luke 21:10; JS—M 1:29). false prophets shall rise, Matt. 24:11 (Mark 13:22). after I am risen again, I will go before you, Matt. 26:32 (Mark 14:28). lest his disciples … say … He is risen from the dead, Matt. 27:64. not here: for he is risen, Matt. 28:6 (Mark 16:6; Luke 24:6). if Satan rise up against himself … he cannot stand, Mark 3:26. the dead, that they rise, Mark 12:26. The Lord is risen, Luke 24:34. Christ to suffer, and to rise from the dead, Luke 24:46. Rise, take up thy bed, and walk, John 5:8. Thy brother shall rise again, John 11:23. knew not the scripture, that he must rise again, John 20:9. In the name of Jesus Christ … rise up and walk, Acts 3:6. be the first that should rise from the dead, Acts 26:23. For to this end Christ both died, and rose, Rom. 14:9. if there be no resurrection of the dead, then is Christ not risen, 1 Cor. 15:13 (15:16; Mosiah 16:7). now is Christ risen from the dead, 1 Cor. 15:20. if the dead rise not at all? why are they then baptized for the dead, 1 Cor. 15:29 (D&C 128:16). baptism, wherein also ye are risen with him, Col. 2:12. If ye then be risen with Christ, Col. 3:1. dead in Christ shall rise first, 1 Thes. 4:16.",
